{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SeDgeQwWVopD39wT8u8GbT","type":"tool_result","content":"docs/paper/sections/analysis.tex:15:This mechanism is analogous to delusional bias \\citep{lu2018nondelusional}, but differs in origin: delusional bias arises from policy-class constraints, while CIVO is model-induced---the reward head's co-adaptation with the temporal embedding produces systematically upward-biased predictions at $\\dt > 1$.  The consequence (policy exploitation of overestimated regions) is similar, but the causal pathway is distinct.\ndocs/paper/sections/analysis.tex:83:[Omitted long matching line]\ndocs/paper/sections/analysis.tex:88:[Omitted long matching line]\ndocs/paper/sections/analysis.tex:98:[Omitted long matching line]\ndocs/paper/sections/analysis.tex:103:[Omitted long matching line]\ndocs/paper/sections/related_work.tex:5:[Omitted long matching line]\ndocs/paper/sections/related_work.tex:8:TAWM \\citep{nhu2025tawm} conditions a world model on $\\dt$ within TD-MPC2 \\citep{hansen2024tdmpc2} and achieves consistent gains. The critical distinction is architectural: TAWM re-plans from real states at every step, so model errors do not accumulate into the critic. We show that identical $\\dt$-conditioning fails in DreamerV3's imagination loop, where errors compound through bootstrapping---transforming manageable imprecision into pathological value overestimation.\ndocs/paper/sections/related_work.tex:11:[Omitted long matching line]\ndocs/paper/sections/methodology.tex:7:All experiments build on DreamerV3 \\citep{hafner2023dreamerv3}, which learns a recurrent state-space model (RSSM) with discrete latent states ($32$ categories $\\times$ $32$ classes), uses symlog-transformed predictions, and trains an actor-critic entirely within imagined trajectories. The standard configuration imagines $H{=}15$ steps at a fixed temporal resolution of $\\dt{=}1$, meaning each imagination step corresponds to one environment transition.\ndocs/paper/sections/methodology.tex:74:Each non-baseline configuration is run with 2--3 seeds. The baseline uses 2 seeds (seeds 1 and 2) to establish reference variance; a third seed (seed 0) is in progress. Following \\citet{agarwal2021precipice}, we report per-seed trajectories rather than aggregated means to surface stochastic divergence across seeds.\ndocs/paper/sections/methodology.tex:104:[Omitted long matching line]\ndocs/paper/sections/introduction.tex:4:TAWM \\citep{nhu2025tawm} shows that conditioning a world model on step size $\\dt$ yields consistent gains within TD-MPC2's MPC framework \\citep{hansen2024tdmpc2}. Can the same $\\dt$-conditioning bring temporal abstraction to imagination-based actor-critic methods like DreamerV3 \\citep{hafner2023dreamerv3}, where policies are trained entirely in imagined rollouts?\ndocs/paper/sections/introduction.tex:6:[Omitted long matching line]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01La2FcbfByTJqmZP1zJJuVh","session_id":"f87adec8-cfa3-4ccb-9dba-1d424d081a40","uuid":"f70f55ef-fb45-4993-bd2a-7fb1c8b11a3e","timestamp":"2026-05-16T12:54:35.457Z"}
